doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22914522"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22914522"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reproducible MoFuSS-based landscape screening for woodfuel pressure,
  conditional biomass recovery, climate exposure and population/poverty context in Congo
  Basin and KAZA. This postprocessor preserves physical quantities,
  model assumptions, scenario distinctions and data coverage. Its outputs
  support prioritization discussions, not site approval, causal intervention
  estimates or carbon-credit accounting.
keywords:
  - restoration
  - MoFuSS
  - woodfuel
  - Congo Basin
  - KAZA
  - spatial prioritization
  - reproducibility
